Usage of ubyte-webssh-bridge:
  -conn-max-per-host int
    	concurrent sessions to one target on the path route, at most -conn-max-total (default 10)
  -conn-max-total int
    	concurrent sessions of the process (default 1000)
  -health
    	dial the listen address and exit 0 when it accepts a TCP connection
  -rate-burst int
    	new sessions one client address opens at once (default 10)
  -rate-interval duration
    	time a client address takes to regain -rate-burst new sessions (default 2s)
  -server-address string
    	TLS listen address, host:port; beyond loopback it needs -ssh-target (default ":8443")
  -server-cert string
    	PEM file of the TLS certificate and its chain (default "/data/certificate.crt")
  -server-debug
    	write the debug records too
  -server-key string
    	PEM file of the TLS private key (default "/data/certificate.key")
  -server-shutdown-timeout duration
    	time the sessions have to end after SIGINT or SIGTERM (default 30s)
  -server-trusted-proxies list
    	IPs and CIDR prefixes of proxies whose X-Forwarded-For and X-Real-IP name the client (default "127.0.0.0/8,::1/128")
  -ssh-connect-timeout duration
    	time to open the TCP connection to the target (default 10s)
  -ssh-login-timeout duration
    	time from the TCP connection to the started shell, the user's answers included (default 2m0s)
  -ssh-target string
    	host:port every session reaches through /ws; empty: /ws/{host}/{port}, on a loopback listener only
  -version
    	print the version and the Go release and exit
  -ws-handshake-timeout duration
    	time a client has to send its request headers and its connect message (default 10s)
